  <running_head>PHYSICARUM LIB. VI.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>non</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">poteft: <i>An calidum innatum queat quo-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>que putrefcere ?</i> Non abfolute impoffi-</l>
    <l n="3">bile eft, quippe miftum corpus eft: &amp;</l>
    <l n="4">forte contingit quandoque, cum cali-</l>
    <l n="5">dum innatum aliis implexum eft: fed</l>
    <l n="6">folitarie ægre omnino fieri crediderim.</l>
    <l n="7">Nimis enim calor prævalet, &amp; propter</l>
    <l n="8">tenuem fubftantiam facile evaporat.</l>
    <l n="9">Rurfus id quæri poteft: <i>An calidum in-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>natum queat tranfmutari?</i> Non facile</l>
    <l n="11">putem ob virtutem magnam: abfolute</l>
    <l n="12">tamen non negem.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">§. 11. Quæftio 13. eft: <i>An calidum in-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>natum fit caufa naturalis interitus?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">Gal. 1. de Marcore c.3. adducit fententiam</l>
    <l n="16">Hippocratis, quod idem calor, qui cor-</l>
    <l n="17">pora producit, eadem interimat, eam-</l>
    <l n="18">que refutat, quod &amp; alii Medici facere</l>
    <l n="19">folent. Attamen licebit eam diftinctio-</l>
    <l n="20">nem adhibere, &amp; falvare Hippocratem.</l>
    <l n="21">Nimirum calidum innatum propria in-</l>
    <l n="22">tentione &amp; perfe corpora format, fir-</l>
    <l n="23">mat &amp; confervat: at indirecta inten-</l>
    <l n="24">tione &amp; per accidens, quatenus corpo-</l>
    <l n="25">ra siccat, illis &amp; fibi interitum affert:</l>
    <l n="26">quod in naturali <i>μαξίνοις</i> contingere</l>
    <l n="27">Medici docent.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">§. 12. Quæftio 14. eft: <i>Quodnam fit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>contrarium calidi innati?</i> Fernel. 1. 4.</l>
    <l n="30">Phyfiolog. c. 1. docet calori naturali</l>
    <l n="31">non</l>
  </main_text>
